## 2. Root Causes of Duplication

| Cause | Details |
|-------|---------|
| Fragmented data consumption | Components independently call small “slice” queries instead of hydrating from a shared store. |
| Partial in‑flight dedupe | A local `fetchOnceMap` exists in `supabase-queries.ts` but only applied to a subset (e.g. public character queries); many getters (profile, credits, subscription, personas) do not use it. |
| Missing snapshot wiring | Snapshot RPC `get_user_snapshot` returns profile, subscription, credits, counts, characters, personas, favorites—but the frontend still re-fetches each individually afterward. |
| Edge function overlap | The chat-management edge function (supabase/functions/chat-management/index.ts) already returns personas list and creditsBalance, but the UI still dispatches separate queries. |
| Granular profile field queries | Multiple narrow selects (username only, timezone only, default_persona_id only) instead of a memoized full profile object cached client-side. |
| Non-coalesced memory fetches | Separate requests for non-auto and auto summaries in tight sequence (see queries in supabase/functions/chat-management/modules/database.ts) then again from UI. |
| Lack of TTL / reactive subscription strategy | Poll/duplicate on navigation instead of subscribing to tables (only some real-time aspects implemented for context). |
| Static reference data uncached | plans, models, tags, credit_packs seldom change but are refetched repeatedly. |

## 3. Snapshot RPC Review

File: `get_user_snapshot`

Current payload includes:
- profile (private)
- latest subscription + plan id (but not expanded plan object)
- credits balance
- counts: favorites, chats, characters, personas
- lightweight character list
- personas list
- favorite_character_ids

Gaps vs. what the UI still re-fetches:
- Missing expanded plan info (plan fields)
- Missing active plans list (pricing page)
- Missing models list (for model selector)
- Missing user_global_chat_settings
- Missing tags (for character filters)
- Missing default_persona enrichment (profile join output could inline persona summary)
- Missing last few chats or chat summaries for dashboard quick load
- Missing user age verification / feature flags (if gating UI)
- Missing aggregated credit_pack_purchases summary (recent purchases count/value)

Because these are absent, downstream components fall back to individual queries.

## 4. Edge Function (chat-management) Bootstrapping

File: index.ts

Provides:
